WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.352
Sara liked to watch the sunset from her skylight.

2
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:23.892
One evening it was especially beautiful. The sky glowed with golden light.

3
00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:29.061
"It's a splendid one," Sara said softly to herself.

4
00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:32.487
Suddenly she heard an odd chattering sound.

5
00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:35.755
She looked toward the skylight next door.

6
00:00:35.756 --> 00:00:41.264
There she saw a dark-skinned man, wearing white clothes and a turban.

7
00:00:41.265 --> 00:00:44.252
He too was looking at the sunset.

8
00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:48.846
The strange noise had come from a little monkey he was holding.

9
00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:55.399
Sara thought the man must be a servant. She also thought he looked sad.

10
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.854
"Perhaps he's homesick," she said to herself.

11
00:00:59.855 --> 00:01:05.810
It was often hot and sunny in India, but here in England, the sun rarely appeared.

12
00:01:05.811 --> 00:01:09.899
He'd probably come up to the roof to catch a glimpse of the sun.

13
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.490
The man suddenly looked at her, and she smiled at him.

14
00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:18.016
She had learned how comforting a smile could be.

15
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:21.584
The man's face lit up, and he smiled back.

16
00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:27.006
At that instant the man's grip on the monkey loosened, and the creature escaped from his arms!

17
00:01:27.007 --> 00:01:32.910
It ran across the roof and down into Sara's room.

18
00:01:32.911 --> 00:01:38.979
Luckily Sara still remembered the language she'd learned while living in India.

19
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.985
The man was delighted to hear someone speaking his language.

20
00:01:42.986 --> 00:01:47.328
"My name is Ram Dass." He bowed to Sara.

21
00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:50.885
"That monkey is nice, but he's a mischievous fellow.

22
00:01:50.886 --> 00:01:54.206
If you'll let me enter your room, I'll capture it."

23
00:01:54.207 --> 00:01:59.280
Sara nodded, and Ram Dass slipped through his skylight.

24
00:01:59.281 --> 00:02:05.751
He easily crossed the steep roof and dropped through her skylight without making a sound.

25
00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:09.963
Within a few moments, he had captured the monkey.

26
00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:14.131
"My master would be very sad to lose his little friend."

27
00:02:14.132 --> 00:02:18.269
Ram Dass patted the monkey. "Thank you, miss."

28
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.348
Ram Dass spoke to Sara very politely.

29
00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:24.739
He treated her as if she weren't a servant.

30
00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.625
She noticed him glancing around her shabby room.

31
00:02:27.626 --> 00:02:31.384
But Ram Dass pretended he'd seen nothing.

32
00:02:31.385 --> 00:02:35.382
Then he bowed once more and disappeared through the skylight.

33
00:02:35.383 --> 00:02:39.924
After Ram Dass left, Sara thought about her life in India.

34
00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:45.686
Only a few years ago, she had been surrounded by servants who treated her with respect.

35
00:02:45.687 --> 00:02:48.474
That all seemed like a dream now.

36
00:02:48.475 --> 00:02:52.114
Sara knew that her life at Miss Minchin's would never improve.

37
00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:54.631
One day she might be a teacher.

38
00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:57.939
But her clothes would still be plain and ugly.

39
00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:03.479
She would still be a servant, and Miss Minchin would still make every day miserable.

40
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.691
Then Sara realized something important.

41
00:03:06.692 --> 00:03:13.938
"Even if I am dressed in rags, I can still act like a princess," she declared.

42
00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:18.142
This thought warmed her cheeks, and she stood up straight.

43
00:03:18.143 --> 00:03:24.368
"It would be easy to be a princess if I were dressed in golden clothing," she told herself.

44
00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:32.293
"But it is a great deal harder to be a princess when I'm dressed like this. I can do this. I know I can!

45
00:03:32.294 --> 00:03:36.627
I must think like a solider marching into battle."

46
00:03:36.628 --> 00:03:41.520
The next morning Sara was in the schoolroom.

47
00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:45.756
She had finished teaching her pupils and was putting away their books.

48
00:03:45.757 --> 00:03:50.747
She thought of a story about a famous king who had lived in disguise.

49
00:03:50.748 --> 00:03:54.857
A shepherd's wife had not known he was a king and slapped him.

50
00:03:54.858 --> 00:04:01.316
The woman must have been very frightened when she found out the truth about the man, Sara thought.

51
00:04:01.317 --> 00:04:07.568
"What would Miss Minchin do if she discovered that I am a princess?" Sara wondered.

52
00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:12.334
Meanwhile Miss Minchin was watching Sara daydreaming.

53
00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:15.044
She hated the look on Sara's face.

54
00:04:15.045 --> 00:04:19.575
It was as if the child were living in a world far away.

55
00:04:19.576 --> 00:04:24.214
Full of rage, Miss Minchin walked over to Sara and slapped her.

56
00:04:24.215 --> 00:04:32.220
Sara was so stunned that something strange happened—she burst out laughing.

57
00:04:32.221 --> 00:04:37.304
"Why are you laughing, you rude child?" Miss Minchin demanded.

58
00:04:37.305 --> 00:04:42.461
Sara took a deep breath. "I was thinking."

59
00:04:42.462 --> 00:04:47.188
"Beg my pardon immediately!" said the headmistress.

60
00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:53.284
Sara hesitated. "I will beg your pardon for laughing," she said.

61
00:04:53.285 --> 00:04:57.330
"But I won't beg your pardon for thinking."

62
00:04:57.331 --> 00:05:01.342
"What were you thinking? How dare you think?"

63
00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:07.621
Jessie and Lavinia giggled, and the other girls looked up from their books.

64
00:05:07.622 --> 00:05:11.912
Sara always had something strange to say to Miss Minchin.

65
00:05:11.913 --> 00:05:14.811
Sara blurted out the truth.

66
00:05:14.812 --> 00:05:19.062
"I was thinking what would happen if I were a princess and you slapped me.

67
00:05:19.063 --> 00:05:22.347
And how shocked and frightened you'd be when you found out."

68
00:05:22.348 --> 00:05:27.083
Every pair of eyes in the room widened in surprise.

69
00:05:27.084 --> 00:05:31.501
"Go to your room this instant!" cried Miss Minchin.

70
00:05:31.502 --> 00:05:33.746
"Back to your lessons, everyone."

71
00:05:33.747 --> 00:05:41.037
Sara left the headmistress shaking with rage and the girls still whispering about her.

72
00:05:41.038 --> 00:05:45.565
"Sara is so strange," Jessie said to Lavinia.

73
00:05:45.566 --> 00:05:55.191
"What if she did turn out to be a princess? I wouldn't be surprised at all!"
